# drive.press with every car file 3 MB larger (tools/port/mods_synth.py's big set): at game.memory original the mods
# raise it, to 32 MiB (8 MiB and six cars' 3 MB), so LoadCars never finds the heap short; the picture is drive's
# (docs/port/MODS.md 5).
# until: 0x400000:900
# seconds: 90
# expect: state=0x00400000: players 1, windows 1, cars 6, mode 0, track 0
# args: --mods-dir mods/big --screenshot-at 1600 --screenshot mods_big.png
# check: tools/port/mods_check.py log mods_big.game.log --has "game.memory raised to 32 MiB" --has "32 MiB of memory (game.memory, for the mods)"
# check: tools/port/heap_check.py mods_big.log --memory 32 --peak-above 17M --short 0
# check: tools/port/mods_check.py same mods_big.png drive.png
5 A            # the controller pak warning
8 START        # the start prompt
11 A           # the main menu: the race
14 A           # the player screen
17 A           # the mode screen: a single race
20 A           # the track select: track 0
23 A           # the car select; the race starts at about 23.6 s and its countdown runs 3.5 s
27 A 20        # gas for 20 s
32 STICKRIGHT 1.5
36 STICKLEFT 1.5
47 B 3         # the brake
